---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Steward
    participant Page as Site page<br/>app/detail/[namesite],<br/>SiteObservationsPanel (proposed)
    participant Server as Server actions<br/>SiteQueries
    participant DB as Supabase DB<br/>sites_pa
    participant INat as iNaturalist API<br/>api.inaturalist.org

    Note over Steward,INat: Covers US 4.0.7. No iNaturalist call exists in the code today.<br/>"(proposed)" = the step is not in the code today.

    Steward->>Page: Open a Site page
    Page->>Server: Read the Site (exists) with its boundary (proposed, US 6.0.1)
    Server->>Server: Check session and approved account (proposed)
    alt No valid session or account not approved
        Server-->>Page: Refuse (401)
        Page-->>Steward: Go to /login
    else Access allowed
        Server->>DB: Read sites_pa row
        DB-->>Server: Site row with boundary
        Server-->>Page: Site with boundary
        Page->>INat: GET /v1/observations with the bounding box of the boundary,<br/>order_by=(popularity measure), per_page=5 (proposed)
        Note over Page,INat: Public read. No iNaturalist account is needed (AT 4).
        alt iNaturalist returns observations
            INat-->>Page: At most 5 observations, with photo, species name and link
            Page-->>Steward: Show at most 5 observations with the species name (AT 1, AT 2, AT 5)
        else No observations
            INat-->>Page: Empty list
            Page-->>Steward: Show "No iNaturalist observations were found" (AT 3)
        else iNaturalist does not respond
            Page-->>Steward: Show that observations are not available. The rest of the page still loads
        end
    end

    Note over Steward,INat: Open questions: the measure of "most popular" (votes, faves or comments),<br/>and if a bounding box is correct for a Site with an irregular shape.<br/>This uses the same browser call as US 4.0.5. It needs the Site boundary from US 6.0.1.
